---
import Divider from "../../../components/ui/Divider.astro";
import Layout from "../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { Code } from "astro-expressive-code/components";

//#region CodeSnippets
const SampleOutput = `
Enter the coefficient a: 1 [Enter]
Enter the coefficient b: -3 [Enter]
Enter the coefficient c: 2 [Enter]
Discriminant: 1
There are two real roots: 2.0 and 1.0

--- run again ---

Enter the coefficient a: 1 [Enter]
Enter the coefficient b: -2 [Enter]
Enter the coefficient c: 1 [Enter]
Discriminant: 0
There is one real root: 1.0

--- run again ---

Enter the coefficient a: 1 [Enter]
Enter the coefficient b: 0 [Enter]
Enter the coefficient c: 1 [Enter]
Discriminant: -4
There are no real roots.
`;
//#endregion
---

<Layout>
  <div class="container my-4">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
      <div class="col-sm-12 col-md-10">
        <a href="/courses/foce/" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-light mb-3">
          <i class="si-arrow-left"></i> Back
        </a>

        <h1>Code Challenge: Quadratics</h1>

        <h4>
          Difficulty&nbsp;&nbsp;
          <i class="si-star text-sn-green"></i>
        </h4>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="mb-5" />

        <section id="objective">
          <h2>Objective</h2>

          <p>
            Solve a quadratic equation <b class="text-sn-cyan"
              >ax<sup>2</sup> + bx + c = 0</b
            > using the quadratic formula.
          </p>

          <p>
            The <b>discriminant</b> is <b class="text-sn-cyan"
              >b<sup>2</sup> &minus; 4ac</b
            >, and its sign decides how many real roots exist. That makes this a
            conditionals problem as much as a maths problem.
          </p>

          <h4>Skills to Practice</h4>

          <ul>
            <li>Prompting a user for input</li>
            <li>Using <code>math.sqrt()</code> from Activity 1.9</li>
            <li>Branching on a value you calculated yourself</li>
            <li>Formatting custom output</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="tasks">
          <h2>Tasks</h2>

          <ul>
            <li>
              Create a new <b>Python</b> program named <b class="text-sn-theme"
                >cc-quadratics.py</b
              >.
            </li>
            <li>Prompt the user for the coefficients a, b, and c.</li>
            <li>Calculate the discriminant and display it.</li>
            <li>
              If it is <b>positive</b>, there are two distinct real roots. Display
              both.
            </li>
            <li>
              If it is <b>zero</b>, there is exactly one real root. Display it.
            </li>
            <li>
              If it is <b>negative</b>, there are no real roots. Say so rather than
              letting the program crash.
            </li>
            <li>
              Root formula: <b class="text-sn-cyan"
                >(&minus;b &plusmn; &radic;discriminant) &divide; 2a</b
              >
            </li>
          </ul>

          <p class="mt-3">
            Test all three branches. Try <b>a=1, b=-3, c=2</b> for two roots,{" "}
            <b>a=1, b=-2, c=1</b> for one, and <b>a=1, b=0, c=1</b> for none. If
            you only ever test the first, you will never find out that{" "}
            <code>math.sqrt()</code> crashes on a negative number.
          </p>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="sample-output">
          <h2>Sample Output</h2>

          <Code
            code={SampleOutput}
            frame="terminal"
            title="Sample Output"
            lang="txt"
            showLineNumbers={false}
            class="mt-3"
          />
        </section>

        <h1
          class="text-center mt-5 text-sn-theme border border-primary slow-flash"
        >
          Commence Challenge
        </h1>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
